## start_group_combat_encounter
Roll Initiative once for every living creature taking part in a group encounter. Supply all player characters, GM-controlled companions, and hostiles that are present when combat starts. The engine owns the resulting order; never omit a present companion merely to fit the two-creature encounter operation. Coordinate combat requires a saved spatial scene. For the first encounter, supply one scene in combat_scenes using the spatial_scene format 1 content definition: format=1; map with id, revision, bounds.min/max (three coordinates), grid.cell_size/unit='ft'/origin (two coordinates), and layers (id/min_elevation/max_elevation); entities, geometry, zones and terrain arrays. Each combatant needs exactly one active creature body: id, map_id, position (three coordinates), footprint (box.half_extents or circle.radius), height, facing (two coordinates), active, movement, visibility, and metadata with participant_ref equal to its saved actor ID, creature_type, plane and lighting. Choose physical positions and body dimensions from the encounter fiction; do not invent a target-distance substitute. Include known blockers and terrain. Declare metadata.player.label/kind only on bodies and geometry the player knows. Coordinate combat uses the saved spatial scene. Supply one combat_scenes entry when admitting a later roster or an actual new arena. Omit it to reuse the scene. For the same map ID, keep the existing bounds, grid and layers: all saved bodies, objects, blockers, zones and terrain remain authoritative; supplied rows with existing IDs do not edit or relocate them. New IDs add genuinely present scene facts. For a new map ID, explicitly place every accompanying saved body/object by its exact ID. Existing dimensions, activity and mechanic metadata are retained; only actual destination position, facing, plane and ambient lighting are admitted. Include active summons, carried/worn objects, and a live Mage Hand with its cargo and caster. Arena replacement is unavailable while an anchored object, wall panel including permanent Stone, retained coordinate area/terrain or anchored light needs its current scene. Those effects are preserved and the operation clearly rejects before initiative; do not remove them or substitute a different map ID to bypass this limit. Exploration does not require map movement.
arguments: {
 combat_scenes?: object[] // min items 0; max items 1
 combatants: string[] // min items 3; max items 16; unique
 known_spell_effect?: boolean
 // Monk combatants choosing Uncanny Metabolism when Initiative is rolled: regain all Focus and heal Monk level plus the Martial Arts die, once per Long Rest. Leave empty to decline; eligible level-15 Monks then receive Perfect Focus automatically.
 uncanny_metabolism_users?: string[] // min items 0; max items 16; unique
 // Declare what remains of the exact current player request after this preparation succeeds. Use unresolved_action if an attack or other action was declared and still needs resolution; omission has that same meaning. Use await_player_choice only when the request ends at preparation, such as establishing Initiative before the player chooses an action. Never use it to abandon an already-declared action or invent the player's next choice. This is provider-only control, not a Ruleset or Campaign State field.
 player_intent_after_preparation?: "unresolved_action" | "await_player_choice"
}

## record_srd_scene_hand_occupancy
Record actual hands and grasps for this body without changing equipment or Somatic facts.
arguments: {
 // Exact state entity ID for actor_state from SYLVIA_GM_CAMPAIGN_PREPARATION or SYLVIA_GM_FRESH_CAMPAIGN_STATE; never use a display name.
 actor_state: string // a entity id
 hand_capacity: integer // >= 0; <= 8
 holdings: {
  hand_indices: integer[] // unique
  inventory_item: string // min length 1
 }[] // max items 9
}

## complete_srd_rest
Complete a tracked rest after the clock and activity requirements are met. Restore encoded class resources or NPC per-day spells; a Long Rest also restores HP and Hit Dice, removes ordinary Temporary HP and reduces recoverable Exhaustion. Short Rest Hit Dice remain a separate player choice. Missing resource maxima are never invented.
arguments: {
 known_spell_effect?: boolean
 // Exact participant_id for target_character from SYLVIA_GM_CAMPAIGN_PREPARATION or SYLVIA_GM_FRESH_CAMPAIGN_STATE; never use a display name.
 target_character?: string // a participant id
 // Exact state entity ID for target_state from SYLVIA_GM_CAMPAIGN_PREPARATION or SYLVIA_GM_FRESH_CAMPAIGN_STATE; never use a display name.
 target_state: string // a entity id
}

## take_srd_short_rest_hit_die
Immediately after a tracked Short Rest completes, spend one Hit Die and apply its healing. Choose further dice after each result, before advancing time or resuming other activity. For mixed class pools, ask which class's die to spend and supply hit_die_class. Omit it for older single-die characters or a single class pool.
arguments: {
 hit_die_class?: string
 // Exact state entity ID for target_state from SYLVIA_GM_CAMPAIGN_PREPARATION or SYLVIA_GM_FRESH_CAMPAIGN_STATE; never use a display name.
 target_state: string // a entity id
}

## record_srd_hand_sized_form
Classify a fictional trinket or image as fitting this actual caster's hand, with its admitted depiction geometry.
arguments: {
 // Exact state entity ID for caster_state from SYLVIA_GM_CAMPAIGN_PREPARATION or SYLVIA_GM_FRESH_CAMPAIGN_STATE; never use a display name.
 caster_state: string // a entity id
 extent: number[] // min items 3; max items 3
 fiction: string
 form_id: string
 kind: "trinket" | "image"
}

## record_srd_spell_material_object
Link one actual prepared sapphire material lot to its actual carried scene object.
arguments: {
 // Exact state entity ID for caster_state from SYLVIA_GM_CAMPAIGN_PREPARATION or SYLVIA_GM_FRESH_CAMPAIGN_STATE; never use a display name.
 caster_state: string // a entity id
 material_item_id: string
 object_id: string
}

